# not from a tape — written for the app, so there is no v1 line to match.
@segment  announcement
@title    What This Session Is
@levels   F1
@verbosity 3
@duration ~70s
@from     F1

# Verbosity 3: everything named -- what was chosen, where we are going, what is
# known about it, what the route is, and roughly how long it takes. See
# announcement.v1.gws for how the tokens work.
#
# This does NOT use [[destinationLine]], which v2 does. Where a level has a
# published description, that token and [[destinationPublished]] resolve to the
# same sentence, and v3 spoke it twice six seconds apart -- once plainly and
# once after "what has been written about it". v2 has only the one line and
# still uses it.

say This session is set to verbosity three. Every level named, and what is known about each of them.
pause 4
say We are going to [[destination]].
pause 5
say What has been written about it: [[destinationPublished]]
pause 6
say The way there passes through [[stations]], and takes about [[duration]].
pause 5
say None of this is a prescription. It is a description of where we are going, offered so that you can recognise it if you arrive.
pause 5
say When you are ready, we begin.
pause 6
